ue diagram"],"qpPage":15,"msPage":15,"ctxPage":14,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-q4b","p":7,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(b)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"Patrick Street Productions produces musicals. Its latest production is ‘It’s a Wonderful Life’ and the total cost of this production is $200 000. The ticket price is $40. The theatre has a capacity of 300 seats. The company aims for revenue maximisation. If this is achieved, revenue from ticket sales will cover 30% of total costs. Charitable donations contribute 12.5% towards total cost and a government subsidy ensures the production covers all of its costs. Calculate the value of the government subsidy necessary for this production to cover all of its costs.","topics":["3-3-2-costs","1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1","theme-3"],"keywords":["subsidy","total costs","calculation","theatre"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":9,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 4 as printed"},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2021-nov-q6a","p":7,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(a)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":5,"questionText":"Explain the likely impact of diminishing marginal productivity of labour on cabin crew staffing levels. Refer to Extract A in your answer.","topics":["3-5-1-demand-for-labour","3-3-2-costs"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["diminishing marginal productivity","demand for labour","cabin crew","airlines"],"qpPage":16,"msPage":11,"ctxPage":14,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2021-nov-q2c","p":25,"section":"B","questionNumber":"2(c)","parentQuestion":"2","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"Discuss the likely impact of investment in new technology on the profitability of firms in Germany, as described in Extract C line 20. Use a cost and revenue diagram to support your answer.","topics":["2-2-3-investment","3-3-2-costs"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-2","theme-3"],"keywords":["investment","technology","productivity","profitability"],"qpPage":22,"msPage":17,"ctxPage":20,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2020-oct-q4a","p":8,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(a)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"The following illustrates the daily average cost curve for a doughnut producer: Explain what happens to total cost at output levels greater than Z.","topics":["3-3-2-costs"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["average cost","total cost","cost curves"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2020-oct-q4b","p":8,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(b)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"The following illustrates the daily average cost curve for a doughnut producer: At output levels greater than Z, which one of the following correctly identifies what will happen to the cost?","topics":["3-3-2-costs"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["average cost","diseconomies","doughnut producer"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":8,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":null,"usesFigure":true},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2020-oct-q4c","p":8,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(c)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"The following illustrates the daily average cost curve for a doughnut producer: For a luxury doughnut producer the average selling price is £2. The average variable cost is 40% of the selling price and its fixed cost per day is £300. Calculate total costs per day assuming it produces 400 doughnuts per day.","topics":["3-3-2-costs"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["total costs","fixed costs","variable costs","calculation"],"qpPage":6,"msPage":8,"ctxPage":5,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 4 as printed"},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2020-oct-q2c","p":26,"section":"B","questionNumber":"2(c)","parentQuestion":"2","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"Discuss factors that are causing many high street retailers in the UK to close some branches or shut down completely. Use a cost and revenue diagram to support your answer.","topics":["3-3-2-costs","3-3-4-normal-profits-supernormal-profits-losses"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["high street","retail","costs","shut-down point"],"qpPage":22,"msPage":19,"ctxPage":21,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2019-jun-q4b","p":2,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(b)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"In 2016, the insurance group Esure undertook a demerger with its GoCompare price comparison website. Following the demerger, GoCompare announced in 2017 a profit of £17.5 million, up 21.5% on 2016. Total revenue in 2017 was £75.8 million, up 4.1% on 2016. Calculate, using the information provided, the total costs of GoCompare in 2016.","topics":["3-3-2-costs","3-3-4-normal-profits-supernormal-profits-losses","3-3-1-revenue"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3"],"keywords":["total costs","profit","total revenue","calculation"],"qpPage":7,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p3-2018-jun-q2b","p":19,"section":"B","questionNumber":"2(b)","parentQuestion":"2","choiceGroup":null,"marks":8,"questionText":"Examine the likely effects on the profitability of Indonesian rice farmers of the government’s increased investment in dams (Extract E, lines 43-48). Use a cost and revenue diagram to support your answer.","topics":["3-3-2-costs","4-3-3-strategies-influencing-growth-development"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-3","theme-4"],"keywords":["costs","infrastructure","irrigation","rice farmers"],"qpPage":23,"msPage":15,"ctxPage":21,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2017-jun-q4a","p":0,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(a)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"In 2015 JCB, the construction equipment manufacturer, experienced a 6% fall in revenue. This resulted from a reduction in sales of constru